From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 21:56:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] LvglDisplayEngineDxe: Draw the orbs of the wallpaper with no
 circle mask

The orbs of the wallpaper are squares of twice their radius with
LV_RADIUS_CIRCLE, filled with a radial gradient from their center, in
the color of the orb, to the edge of the circle, where it is
transparent; LV_GRAD_EXTEND_PAD keeps it transparent beyond. The circle
mask only clips pixels that are transparent already, and costs a mask
as large as the orb wherever the wallpaper is redrawn: up to 669 px at
a screen height of 1080 px, 1004 px at 1620 px, where the mask of LVGL
v9.5.0 ran off its buffer (previous patch).

Leave the orbs square: the wallpaper looks the same, without the mask.
The other rounded objects of the setup, and their shadows, have a
radius of at most 16 px at 1x and 32 px at 2x (THEME_RADIUS_TILE,
THEME_RADIUS_DOCK).

TEST=QEMU q35 at 2880x1620 (tools/qemu-smoke.py --setup-only --size
2880x1620 of ouroBIOS, at every build): the setup opens and answers the
keys at the four UI scales; at 1920x1080 the wallpaper differs from
v1.3.10-rc3's by at most 2 levels per color.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv

---
 LvglDisplayEngineDxe/LvglDesktop.c | 10 ++++++----
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/LvglDisplayEngineDxe/LvglDesktop.c b/LvglDisplayEngineDxe/LvglDesktop.c
index 1ca8c9a..7de8576 100644
--- a/LvglDisplayEngineDxe/LvglDesktop.c
+++ b/LvglDisplayEngineDxe/LvglDesktop.c
@@ -1,8 +1,11 @@
 /** @file
   Desktop wallpaper of the setup: drawn, not stored. A vertical sky gradient
-  across the screen and three soft orbs of color over it, each a circle
-  filled with a radial gradient that fades to transparent at its edge, so
-  that they blend into the sky and into each other. The palette follows the
+  across the screen and three soft orbs of color over it, each a square
+  filled with a radial gradient that fades to transparent at the edge of its
+  inscribed circle, so that they blend into the sky and into each other.
+  The squares are not rounded: outside that circle the gradient is
+  transparent already, and the circle mask of LVGL can fail at the radius
+  of an orb on a tall screen (1004 px at 1620 px). The palette follows the
   hour of the day, like a dynamic desktop: night, dawn, day, dusk and
   evening. Nothing is animated: the wallpaper only changes when the hour
   moves into another band, and the objects are only redrawn where the
@@ -195,7 +198,6 @@ DesktopBuild (
       (HorRes * mOrbPlaces[Index].CenterXPct) / 100 - Radius,
       (VerRes * mOrbPlaces[Index].CenterYPct) / 100 - Radius
       );
-    lv_obj_set_style_radius (Orb, LV_RADIUS_CIRCLE, 0);
     lv_obj_clear_flag (Orb, LV_OBJ_FLAG_CLICKABLE);
     lv_obj_clear_flag (Orb, LV_OBJ_FLAG_SCROLLABLE);
     lv_obj_add_flag (Orb, LV_OBJ_FLAG_IGNORE_LAYOUT);
